<title>ITALY: Milk, motorways on agenda of Italy cabinet meeting.</title>
<headline>Milk, motorways on agenda of Italy cabinet meeting.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's cabinet will meet on Thursday at 0730 GMT with an agenda including a bitter row over EU fines for milk overproduction and the privatisation of the country's motorway operator, government sources said.</p>
<p>The government has said it will present a decree law outlining cheap loans and grants to farmers hit by EU &quot;super-levy&quot; fines totalling some 370 billion lire ($230 million) and a restructuring of the milk sector.</p>
<p>The fines are due to be paid by Friday, but farmers refuse, saying the government is responsible for the overproduction. They have staged two weeks of protests to press their demands.</p>
<p>Other items on the agenda include a report from the Treasury Ministry on the privatisation of the Autostrade company, which operates Italy's motorways and a series of fiscal measures for the banking sector.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
